<!-- ---- ABOUT ---- -->\
<div class="page" id="about" role="tabpanel">\
  <section class="abhero"><div class="wrap"><h2>About the National Union</h2></div></section>\
\
  <div class="wrap">\
    <div class="about-body">\
      <div class="lede">A debating society for American high schools</div>\
      <svg class="flr" width="66" height="14" viewBox="0 0 66 14" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 7 C 14 -1, 20 15, 33 7 C 46 -1, 52 15, 63 7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>\
\
      <p>The National Union brings free speech, open argument, and critical thinking into American high schools. At every meeting, members take a contested question in politics, ethics, or current affairs and debate it from both sides, examining it below the surface and testing their own views against people who see it differently.</p>\
\
      <p>The National Union grew out of a society founded at Seattle Academy in 2025. A small group of students who were drawn to large, difficult questions found no place in school to discuss them across different friend groups and backgrounds, so they started one. The school was initially resistant: wary of controversy and reluctant to host arguments that might offend, the administration moved to delay and then to close the society, which was established only after its founders pressed to keep it running.</p>\
\
      <p>Once the society was established, its founders created the National Union to bring it to other schools. Each chapter is student-led and follows the same standing orders, and any high school in the country can start one.</p>\
\
      <p>Debates are held at every meeting, with the floor open to any member and no sign-up required to speak. The National Union takes no position of its own; members argue every side of a question, and the room votes before and after, with the result going to whichever side changes more minds. Some members come to sharpen how they argue, others to get more comfortable speaking in front of a room, and many simply to spend an hour in a genuine conversation with people they disagree with.</p>\
\
      <p class="lks">See the <a class="lk" href="#" data-goto="schedule">Schedule</a> for what is coming up, or the <a class="lk" href="#" data-goto="archive">Archive</a> for how past debates were decided.</p>\
\
      <p>Joining the National Union gives you a place to argue hard questions with people who see them differently, and to work through them in the open. We would be glad to have you.</p>\
\
      <div class="about-cta"><button class="bigjoin" id="aboutJoin">Join the National Union</button></div>\
      <div class="about-sub">No chapter at your school yet? <button id="aboutReq">Start one.</button></div>\
    </div>\
  </div>\
</div>\
\
