<!-- ---- RULES ---- -->\
<div class="page" id="rules" role="tabpanel"><div class="wrap">\
  <div class="ph"><div class="k">Standing orders \'b7 rev. 1</div><h2>Rules of procedure</h2>\
</div>\
\
  <h3 class="sec">1 \'b7 The gavel</h3>\
  <div class="gavel">\
    <div class="gv"><div class="st">|</div><div class="wt">One strike</div><div class="sm">The speaker should finish their current sentence and conclude.</div></div>\
    <div class="gv"><div class="st">||</div><div class="wt">Two strikes</div><div class="sm">The speaker's time has ended and they should stop.</div></div>\
  </div>\
  <p class="note">The chair signals with the gavel rather than interrupting verbally. The chair explains the gavel during the opening at the first meeting of the year.</p>\
\
  <h3 class="sec gap">2 \'b7 Order of proceedings</h3>\
  <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.1</div><div><div class="rt">The timer is displayed to the whole room</div><div class="rw">The countdown runs on the room's screen, visible to every member.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.2</div><div><div class="rt">Each side gives an opening before open forum begins</div><div class="rw">The proposition speaks first, then the opposition, each without interruption. Open forum follows.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.3</div><div><div class="rt">A member may not take two consecutive turns in open forum</div><div class="rw">At least one other person must speak between any member's turns. The chair may call on a speaker who has not yet contributed.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.4</div><div><div class="rt">Floor contributions are statements, not questions</div><div class="rw">A member using floor time makes an argument rather than asking a question. Each contribution is limited to 45 seconds.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.5</div><div><div class="rt">Speakers are not required to respond to any given floor contribution</div><div class="rw">Speakers choose which floor points to address. What is raised and what is answered is recorded in the log.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.6</div><div><div class="rt">The proposition delivers the final closing</div><div class="rw">Closings run opposition first, then proposition.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.7</div><div><div class="rt">The chair marks the transition between open-forum blocks</div><div class="rw">Between the two open-forum blocks the chair restates the motion and summarizes where the disagreement stands. No vote is taken.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.8</div><div><div class="rt">Floor rounds absorb changes to timing</div><div class="rw">The chair may add a fourth floor contribution when ahead of schedule, or reduce a round to two when behind. A floor round is not cut in favor of a main speaker.</div></div></div>\
    <div class="rule-row"><div class="rk">2.9</div><div><div class="rt">Two floor speakers are arranged in advance</div><div class="rw">Before each debate the chair arranges for two members to speak first when the floor opens.</div></div></div>\
  </div>\
\
  <h3 class="sec gap">3 \'b7 Voting</h3>\
  <div class="rows">\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">3.1 Method</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">Private ballot by QR code<small>Members vote through a form linked by a QR code on the room's screen.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">3.2 Timing</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">Once before, once after<small>The room votes at the opening and at the close. There is no midpoint vote.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">3.3 Result</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">Decided by the larger change in the vote<small>The side that shifts more of the room between the two votes wins, regardless of the final majority. The result is announced and recorded in the archive.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
  </div>\
\
  <h3 class="sec gap">4 \'b7 Speaker selection</h3>\
  <div class="rows">\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">4.1 Qualifying</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">Drawn from the floor log<small>Speaking slots are offered to members whose floor contributions have been recorded in the log.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">4.2 Reserved slot</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">One slot per debate for a first-time speaker<small>Of the four speaking positions, one is held for a member who has not previously spoken.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">4.3 Rotation</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">A speaker sits out the next two debates<small>After speaking, a member is not eligible for a speaking slot for the next two debates.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">4.4 Confirmation</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">A one-line thesis, 48 hours before<small>Selected speakers submit one sentence stating their position two days before the debate. A speaker who does not confirm is replaced by the reserve.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
    <div class="row"><div class="d">4.5 Non-attendance</div><div class="m" style="font-size:17px">Two additional debates before eligibility<small>A speaker who fails to appear without notice sits out two debates beyond the standard rotation.</small></div><div class="s"></div></div>\
  </div>\
</div></div>\
